<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <section id="terms-page" class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-warning/25 bg-warning/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-warning-foreground">
          Draft—legal review required
        </span>
        <span class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Private-alpha placeholder · 14 September 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-6xl">
        Private-alpha terms
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        These preliminary terms describe the intended evaluation boundary. They are not a substitute for a reviewed pilot agreement and must be approved by qualified counsel before external use.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 border-t border-border pt-10 text-base leading-7">
        <section aria-labelledby="terms-access">
          <h2 id="terms-access" class="text-xl font-semibold">Selective evaluation access</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Applying does not guarantee an invitation. If invited, access will be limited to named design-partner users and may be suspended or withdrawn while the product is being evaluated. There is no public registration or paid plan in this stage.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="terms-purpose">
          <h2 id="terms-purpose" class="text-xl font-semibold">Evaluation purpose</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            The alpha is intended to test whether deterministic output contracts can provide useful regression evidence for bounded LLM workflows. It is not a production service-level commitment or a guarantee that every regression, quality change, or provider incident will be detected.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="terms-responsibility">
          <h2 id="terms-responsibility" class="text-xl font-semibold">
            Participant responsibility
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Participants remain responsible for reviewing results, deciding whether test cases and contracts represent their requirements, controlling what data they submit, and independently validating changes before acting on them in production.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="terms-sensitive-data">
          <h2 id="terms-sensitive-data" class="text-xl font-semibold">Sensitive data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Do not submit regulated, highly sensitive, or third-party confidential data unless a reviewed pilot agreement and appropriate safeguards explicitly permit it. Provider credentials must only be supplied through the product credential flow once that flow is enabled—not through public forms or ordinary messages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="terms-changes">
          <h2 id="terms-changes" class="text-xl font-semibold">Changes and pilot agreement</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
            Product scope and these preliminary terms may change during the alpha. A separate reviewed agreement should define confidentiality, ownership, warranty, liability, data processing, termination, and governing-law terms before a real external pilot begins.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
